<article class="env-lemma" id="0D11">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D11">Lemma <span data-tag="0D11">76.21.7</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is formally étale, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}) = H^0(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}) = 0$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume (1). A formally étale morphism is a formally smooth morphism. Thus $H^{-1}(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{X/Y}) = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0D10" data-tag="0D10">76.21.6</a>. On the other hand, a formally étale morphism if formally unramified hence we have $\Omega _{X/Y} = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/04G9" data-tag="04G9">76.14.6</a>. Conversely, if (2) holds, then $f$ is formally smooth by Lemma <a href="/tag/0D10" data-tag="0D10">76.21.6</a> and formally unramified by Lemma <a href="/tag/04G9" data-tag="04G9">76.14.6</a> and hence formally étale by Lemmas <a href="/tag/061G" data-tag="061G">76.19.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>